The user flagged uncertainty about whether origin/HEAD needs to have
been merged as the final step for the range to be correct. It does
not — origin/HEAD..HEAD captures the original branch commits as long
as they don't predate origin/HEAD in the upstream graph, which they
can't for a feature branch. Merging origin/HEAD last is still
recommended (the skill says so), but it is not a correctness
requirement for this command.
